From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:07:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: calibrate the sg-pc profile for STEINS;GATE (Steam)

TYN-only. Switch the profile to InstructionSet.SGHD and replace the Chaos;Child art definitions with
measured S;G ones where they are needed to see the game:
  - sprites.lua: sheets by system.mpk id (DATA01 6, FONT 9, BACKLOG 2, BLOGMASK 3, TITLE_CHIP 30);
  - hud/titlemenu.lua: the CC title menu class (same structure: START/LOAD/EXTRA/CONFIG/HELP, LOAD and EXTRA
    sub lists) fed with the S;G title sheet: the 1920x1080 background at (0,0), main entries at x=1922/2123,
    sub entries 249x37 at x=1957/2245, orange pointer, "Press Enter"; the CC specific layers are neutralised
    with a transparent block. Screen positions of the entries are estimates;
  - dialogue.lua: the ADV box is DATA01 (1150,1206 1921x330) at y=750;
  - font.lua: the font sheet is 64x125 cells (3072x6000), not 64x117;
  - scriptvars.lua: SW_MESWIN0TYPE moves to an unused block (4422 is the second mask priority in S;G; the
    scripts write 34 there, which switched the dialogue text off);
  - the remaining copied CC HUD sprites (save icon, loading, date, system message, selection, backlog, tips)
    point at a transparent block until their S;G art is measured.
Verified on MuMu (Android 15): logos, title, menu, START, the opening scene with its dialogue text.

